{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Game Class Lifecycle.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Game Class Lifecycle.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"game class lifecycle game class lifecycle","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Game Class Lifecycle.md","fileName":"Game Class Lifecycle.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Game Class Lifecycle","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-20 23:34\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[C++ Game Engine Architecture]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["C++ Game Engine Architecture","Game Loop","gameprogrammingincplusplus.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Game Class Lifecycle.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Game Class Lifecycle.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"game class lifecycle game class lifecycle","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Game Class Lifecycle.md","fileName":"Game Class Lifecycle.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Game Class Lifecycle","heading":"Game Class Lifecycle","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A game class lifecycle coordinates initialization, the main [[Game Loop]], and shutdown through one owning object. Initialization creates subsystems and loads data; the loop processes input, updates state, and renders; shutdown releases game data before the libraries it depends on.\n\nKeeping those phases explicit makes partial failure manageable. If initialization stops midway, the game can release only the resources that were successfully created rather than relying on process termination.","tags":["baby"],"links":["C++ Game Engine Architecture","Game Loop","gameprogrammingincplusplus.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Game Class Lifecycle.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Game Class Lifecycle.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"game class lifecycle game class lifecycle","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Game Class Lifecycle.md","fileName":"Game Class Lifecycle.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Game Class Lifecycle","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[gameprogrammingincplusplus.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["C++ Game Engine Architecture","Game Loop","gameprogrammingincplusplus.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}